1. Display          Used for the largest, most prominent text on a screen (like a hero header).
displayLarge (57sp)
displayMedium (45sp)
displaySmall (36sp)

2. Headline             Used for high-emphasis text that marks primary sections of a page.
headlineLarge (32sp)
headlineMedium (28sp)
headlineSmall (24sp)

3. Title                  Used for medium-emphasis text, like the title of a card or a top app bar.
titleLarge (22sp)
titleMedium (16sp)
titleSmall (14sp)

4. Body                 Used for long-form writing and the majority of the UI's content.
bodyLarge (16sp)
bodyMedium (14sp)
bodySmall (12sp)

5. Label                     Used for small, functional text like components (buttons) or captions (tags).
labelLarge (14sp)
labelMedium (12sp)
labelSmall (11sp)